<article class="env-example" id="0FLK">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0FLK">Example <span data-tag="0FLK">20.29.4</span>.</a> Let $(X, \mathcal{O}_ X)$ be a ringed space. Let $\mathcal{F}^\bullet $ be a complex of $\mathcal{O}_ X$-modules. We can apply Lemma <a href="/tag/0BKK" data-tag="0BKK">20.29.1</a> with $F^ p\mathcal{F}^\bullet = \sigma _{\geq p}\mathcal{F}^\bullet $. Then we get a spectral sequence </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  E_1^{p, q} = H^{p + q}(X, \mathcal{F}^ p[-p]) = H^ q(X, \mathcal{F}^ p)  \]
</div>
  <p> If $\mathcal{F}^\bullet $ is bounded below, then </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
we can use Remark <a href="/tag/0BKL" data-tag="0BKL">20.29.2</a> to construct this spectral sequence, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
the spectral sequence is bounded and converges to $H^{i + j}(X, \mathcal{F}^\bullet )$, and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
the spectral sequence is equal to the first spectral sequence of Derived Categories, Lemma <a href="/tag/015J" data-tag="015J">13.21.3</a> (constructed using Cartan-Eilenberg resolutions). 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article>